/-!
# Scaling divisors with independent coefficients have a single null ray

Let `X` be a projective `ℚ`-factorial normal complex variety with canonical divisor `K`, `(X, B)`
a real klt pair, and `H = ∑ⱼ hⱼ Hⱼ` with `ℚ`-Cartier `ℚ`-divisors `Hⱼ` whose classes span
`N¹(X)_ℝ` and real coefficients `hⱼ` linearly independent over the subfield `k₀ ⊆ ℝ` generated by
the coefficients of `B`. For `λ > 0`, the numerical classes of the curves `C` with
`(K + B + λ H) · C = 0` all lie on one ray of `N₁(X)_ℝ`: writing `a = -(K + B) · C ∈ k₀`, the
relation `λ ∑ⱼ hⱼ (Hⱼ · C) = a` with rational `Hⱼ · C` forces `a ≠ 0`, and eliminating `λ`
between two null curves gives `a' [C] = a [C']` by independence and spanning.

If moreover `R` is a `(K + B)`-negative extremal ray of `NE̅(X)` that is null for `K + B + λ H`,
`f : X ⟶ Z` its contraction and `X ⟶ Z ⟵ X⁺` a real flip of it, then on `X⁺` no
`(K⁺ + B⁺)`-negative extremal ray of `NE̅(X⁺)` is null for `K⁺ + B⁺ + λ H⁺`, where `B⁺`, `H⁺` are
the strict transforms: the flipped curve is null and `(K⁺ + B⁺)`-positive, and the hypotheses of
the first part persist on `X⁺`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_pos_smul_numericalClass_eq_of_linearIndependent`.

## Implementation notes

The linear form `u ↦ (D · u)` on `N₁(X)_ℝ` of an `ℝ`-divisor `D` is computed through a
presentation `D = ∑ rⱼ Lⱼ` by Cartier divisors `Lⱼ`, as `∑ rⱼ deg_u 𝒪_X(Lⱼ)`; the value does not
depend on the presentation, and every hypothesis asks for one presentation, every conclusion
excludes all of them. A curve is null when this form vanishes on its class, and a ray is negative
or null when the form is negative, resp. zero, on its nonzero vectors. That the classes of the
`Hⱼ` span `N¹(X)_ℝ` is stated on representatives: every `ℝ`-Cartier divisor is numerically
equivalent to a real combination of the `Hⱼ`. The field `k₀` is the subfield of `ℝ` generated by
the coefficients of `B`; the integral divisor `K` adds nothing to it. The flip is a step of an
extremal real flip sequence `MMP.Fourfold.IsRealFlipStep` of the contraction of `R`, with
`B⁺ = (f⁺)⁻¹_* f_* B`, and `H⁺` the strict transform of `H`.

## References

* [OpenAI, *Termination for projective log canonical fourfolds with rational boundary*][OAI4]
-/

@[expose] public section

section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry MMP.Mori MMP.Flips MMP.Fourfold
